{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "latlon3d_transport_cwc_freestream",
    "description": "CONSISTENCY WITH CONTINUITY (CWC) / FREE-STREAM PRESERVATION on latlon3d: the acid test that a CONSTANT tracer stays constant under a STRONGLY DIVERGENT vertical wind -- and stays constant BIT-FOR-BIT, not merely to within rounding. \n\nWHAT IS BROKEN WITHOUT IT. The flux-form advection rule grids/latlon3d/rules/upwind1_flux_D_lev_noflux_bc transports a MIXING RATIO with a prescribed wind: du/dt = -D(W*u, wrt: lev). Put u == 1 into that and the right-hand side is -dW/dz, which is nonzero wherever the wind diverges: a uniform tracer immediately develops structure out of nothing, growing linearly in time. That is not a discretization error -- refining the mesh does not remove it -- it is a MODELLING error. A mixing ratio is a ratio to an air mass, and the model was never carrying the air mass, so nothing in the equation knew that the air itself was being compressed and rarefied. \n\nTHE FIX: CARRY THE MASS. This driver evolves TWO states -- the air mass per unit area m (the pressure thickness dp) and the tracer mass mq -- and defines the mixing ratio as the OBSERVED q = mq / m: \n    d(m)/dt  = -D(M, wrt: lev)        [continuity;  face_flux_divergence_lev_noflux_bc] \n    d(mq)/dt = -D(M*q, wrt: lev)      [tracer;      upwind1_flux_D_lev_noflux_bc, unchanged] \nwith M the face air-mass flux on [lon, lat, lev_nodes]. Two rules, two terms, one model. The tracer rule is reused VERBATIM -- what changed is not the operator but what it is applied to. \n\nWHY q == 1 IS PRESERVED, AND WHY BITWISE. With q == 1 the donor-cell face flux collapses: F = 1/2[M(qL + qR) - |M|(qR - qL)] = 1/2[M*2 - |M|*0] = M. Every step of that collapse is EXACT in IEEE binary floating point -- 1 + 1 = 2 exactly, M*2 exactly (a power-of-two scaling), 1 - 1 = 0 exactly, |M|*0 = 0 exactly, 0.5*(2M) = M exactly -- so F is the mass flux to the LAST BIT, not to within an epsilon. The tracer divergence then differences the same faces, over the same thicknesses, with the same wall fluxes omitted (both rules delete the wall term rather than forming it and multiplying by zero), so it emits the identical double-precision numbers the continuity divergence emits. mq and m therefore see BITWISE IDENTICAL right-hand sides, every Runge-Kutta stage combines bitwise identical values with identical coefficients, and since mq(0) = m(0) by construction, mq == m bitwise for all time. q = mq/m is then the IEEE division of a double by itself: exactly 1.0. The measured max|q - 1| over the trajectory is 0.0. \n\nTHE WIND IS GENUINELY DIVERGENT. M = 4 z (1 - z)(1 - 2z) a(i) b(j) vanishes at BOTH walls -- no air flows through the ground or the lid, which is the only physically admissible choice and also what the no-flux closure assumes -- and reverses sign at z = 1/2, so air converges on the middle of the column from both directions and both branches of the donor-cell selection are exercised in every column. Its divergence 4 - 24z + 24z^2 is nonzero almost everywhere (it is +4 at the walls and -2 at mid-column), so the air mass m moves by up to ~30% of its initial value over the test window: the free-stream property is being tested against a wind that would visibly wreck the naive mixing-ratio scheme, not against a nearly-nondivergent one. The horizontal modulation a(i) b(j) is strictly positive, so it changes the magnitude of the divergence but not the sign pattern, and it means a stencil that mis-indexed M as a column profile would be caught rather than silently agreeing. \n\nTHE ASSERTIONS. The discrete continuity equation here is EXACT: the finite-volume divergence of the exact face fluxes IS the exact cell-mean divergence (fundamental theorem of calculus, no truncation error at any resolution), and the right-hand side is time-independent, so the semi-discrete solution is m(t) = mean(m0) - t * (M_{k+1} - M_k)/dz[k] in closed form. Both m AND mq are asserted against that same closed form at t = 0.1 with a tolerance of 1e-10 -- m because the continuity operator must be right, mq because free-stream preservation says the tracer mass must track the air mass. mq is additionally asserted against m(0) at t = 0 to pin q(0) = 1. (An inline test cannot assert q itself: esm-spec 6.6.5 assertions on an array OBSERVED are evaluated state-free, and q depends on the state. The bit-exactness of q is measured directly from the solver trajectory instead.) \n\nNLON and NLAT are pinned at both rule import edges; NLEV is left LIVE so the loader API can bind it per resolution and so this file's build-time ic/reference expressions can fold z from literals plus NLEV. A metaparameter pinned at an import edge is CONSUMED there and is not a live name in this document's runtime scope, which is why the horizontal extents appear as the literals 8 and 5 inside the runtime expressions for M.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:latlon3d",
      "op:advection",
      "op:div",
      "form:flux",
      "scheme:upwind",
      "axes:lev",
      "bc:no-flux",
      "mms:free-stream"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Jockel, P., von Kuhlmann, R., Lawrence, M. G., et al. (2001). On a fundamental problem in implementing flux-form advection schemes for tracer transport in 3-dimensional general circulation and chemistry transport models. Quarterly Journal of the Royal Meteorological Society, 127(573), 1035-1052.",
        "doi": "10.1002/qj.49712757318"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Lin, S.-J., & Rood, R. B. (1996). Multidimensional flux-form semi-Lagrangian transport schemes. Monthly Weather Review, 124(9), 2046-2070.",
        "doi": "10.1175/1520-0493(1996)124<2046:MFFSLT>2.0.CO;2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Jacobson, M. Z. (2005). Fundamentals of Atmospheric Modeling (2nd ed.). Cambridge University Press. Chapter 6."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "TransportCWCFreeStream": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lev_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 8,
            "NLAT": 5
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/upwind1_flux_D_lev_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 8,
            "NLAT": 5
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "m": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "AIR MASS per unit area in the cell (the pressure thickness dp); cell means. Initialised to the exact cell mean of m*(z) = 2 - z and then evolved by the continuity equation alone -- nothing forces it, so it genuinely moves under the divergent wind."
        },
        "mq": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "TRACER MASS in the cell; cell means. Initialised to mq(0) = m(0), i.e. a mixing ratio of exactly 1 everywhere. Free-stream preservation is the statement that it stays equal to m."
        },
        "pe": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Level-edge coordinate; pe[1] = 0 (ground), pe[NLEV+1] = 1 (model top). Stretched (0.6 s + 0.4 s^2, s = (kn-1)/NLEV) so the vertical mesh is genuinely non-uniform and cells are thin at the ground. Aggregate index `kn`, distinct from an operator's `k` (observeds are inlined non-hygienically).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "kn"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "kn": {
                "from": "lev_nodes"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.6,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.4,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer thicknesses dz[k] = pe[k+1] - pe[k], from the grid's lev_thickness template (aggregate index `gk`). Both the continuity divergence and the tracer flux divergence divide by THIS array, which is one of the three things the free-stream bit-exactness argument depends on (same faces, same thicknesses, same wall omissions).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "lev_thickness",
            "bindings": {
              "pe": "pe"
            }
          }
        },
        "M": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Face AIR-MASS FLUX, positive upward, on the NLEV+1 face axis: M = 4 z (1 - z)(1 - 2z) a(i) b(j). Vanishes EXACTLY at both walls in floating point -- z(1-z) is 0.0 at z = 0 and at z = 1.0, unlike sin(2 pi z), whose model-top value is -2.4e-16 -- and reverses sign at z = 1/2, so the flow converges on mid-column and both donor branches run. Strongly divergent: div(M) = (4 - 24 z + 24 z^2) a(i) b(j), which is +4 a b at the walls and -2 a b at mid-column.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "iw",
              "jw",
              "kw"
            ],
            "args": [
              "pe"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "iw": {
                "from": "lon"
              },
              "jw": {
                "from": "lat"
              },
              "kw": {
                "from": "lev_nodes"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    4.0,
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "pe",
                        "kw"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "-",
                      "args": [
                        1,
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "pe",
                            "kw"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "-",
                      "args": [
                        1,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            2,
                            {
                              "op": "index",
                              "args": [
                                "pe",
                                "kw"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    1,
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        0.25,
                        {
                          "op": "cos",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                6.283185307179586,
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "-",
                                      "args": [
                                        "iw",
                                        0.5
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    8
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    1,
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        0.2,
                        {
                          "op": "sin",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                3.141592653589793,
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "-",
                                      "args": [
                                        "jw",
                                        1
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    4
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "q": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The MIXING RATIO q = mq / m: tracer mass divided by air mass, cell by cell. It is a BARE declared observed of shape [lon, lat, lev], which is exactly what the advection rule's esm-spec 9.6.1 `where` constraint demands -- a shape constraint is satisfied only by a bare variable reference, never by a compound sub-AST, so the equation MUST be written D(M*q) over a declared q rather than D(M*mq/m) inline. This single indirection is the whole of consistency with continuity: the tracer flux is built from the ratio to a mass the model actually carries. Aggregate indices `iq,jq,kq`, distinct from the operator's `i,j,k`.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "iq",
              "jq",
              "kq"
            ],
            "args": [
              "mq",
              "m"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "iq": {
                "from": "lon"
              },
              "jq": {
                "from": "lat"
              },
              "kq": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "mq",
                    "iq",
                    "jq",
                    "kq"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "m",
                    "iq",
                    "jq",
                    "kq"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      },
